.Dd June 11, 2026
.Dt LIBFOLE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libfole.h
.Nd Library to support the Object Linking and Embedding (OLE) data types
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In libfole.h
.Pp
Support functions
.nf
.Ft const char *
.Fo libfole_get_version
.Fa "void"
.Fc
.fi
.Pp
Error functions
.nf
.Ft void
.Fo libfole_error_free
.Fa "libfole_error_t **error"
.Fc
.fi
.nf
.Ft int
.Fo libfole_error_fprint
.Fa "libfole_error_t *error"
.Fa "FILE *stream"
.Fc
.fi
.nf
.Ft int
.Fo libfole_error_sprint
.Fa "libfole_error_t *error"
.Fa "char *string"
.Fa "size_t size"
.Fc
.fi
.nf
.Ft int
.Fo libfole_error_backtrace_fprint
.Fa "libfole_error_t *error"
.Fa "FILE *stream"
.Fc
.fi
.nf
.Ft int
.Fo libfole_error_backtrace_sprint
.Fa "libfole_error_t *error"
.Fa "char *string"
.Fa "size_t size"
.Fc
.fi
.Pp
Value type functions
.nf
.Ft const char *
.Fo libfole_value_type_get_identifier
.Fa "uint32_t value_type"
.Fc
.fi
.nf
.Ft const char *
.Fo libfole_value_type_get_description
.Fa "uint32_t value_type"
.Fc
.fi
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn libfole_get_version
function is used to retrieve the library version.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Most of the functions return NULL or \-1 on error, dependent on the return \
type.
For the actual return values see
.In libfole.h .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
None
.Sh FILES
None
